title: 'bags-list: fix on_idle cursor skipping nodes on weight exhaustion'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `Pallet::on_idle`'s auto-rebag cursor resumed from a count-based split computed before the
    per-item loop ran, so it skipped past nodes the weight meter or a lock stopped the loop from
    actually reaching.

    The cursor is now computed after the loop, from how far it actually got, so it correctly
    resumes at the first node that was skipped.
crates:
- name: pallet-bags-list
  bump: patch
